liquid_glass_renderer 1.0.0-dev.1, vendored into morph as its glass renderer.

Since 2026-10-03 this is morph's own renderer (lib/src/glass/renderer),
tuned freely; it was vendored under example/third_party before. It stays
Apache-2.0 (LICENSE, NOTICE); the third_party/ notices cover adapted
shader code.

Upstream:  https://github.com/whynotmake-it/flutter_liquid_glass
Branch:    release/01-renderer-core
Commit:    ab1c2d294683f7eea6ee8da6c81d5cd0225ee129 (2026-10-02)
Path:      packages/liquid_glass_renderer
License:   Apache-2.0 (LICENSE), copyright Tim Lehmann for whynotmake.it;
           third_party/ keeps the Flutter (BSD) and Inigo Quilez (MIT)
           notices for adapted shader code.

Copied: LICENSE, lib/, third_party/; hook/build.dart and the shader
bundle manifest moved to the morph package root (hook/build.dart,
morph_glass.shaderbundle.json), the shaders to shaders/ here, the
dependencies and the shader asset list to morph's pubspec.yaml.
Left out: README.md, CHANGELOG.md, pubspec.yaml, doc/, example/, test/,
coverage/, analysis_options.yaml (it includes lintervention, a dev
dependency of the upstream repo). The sources are upstream's except for
the local patches listed below.

Update history:
- cbbac8453c4e023a2bc3b2fd7a2f06e8652e1bf7 (2026-10-01): first vendoring.
- ab1c2d2 (2026-10-02, release/01-renderer-core head on 2026-10-03):
  default frost 3.7 -> 2.0 pt and ios27RegularFrost refitted
  (2 * exp(2.23 * min(t, 0.5) + 2 * max(t - 0.5, 0)): 2 / 6.1 / 16.6 pt
  at slider 0 / 0.5 / 1); glint dimmed to 0.8 in the dark toolbar
  preset and 0.6 in the clear preset; the real and fake glass layers
  share one render base (LiquidGlassRenderObject, GlassFrameState);
  the fake glass backdrop-edge shader removed (Impeller coverage
  workaround). No API change the gallery uses. Upstream's
  LiquidGlassLoupe (re-renders its source at magnified resolution) and
  LoupeTabBar are EXAMPLE code there, not part of the package, and were
  already present at cbbac845; the renderer itself never enlarges its
  backdrop (backdropShrink is clamped to 0..0.75).

Local patches (each its own commit, revertable alone):
- 2026-10-03 backdropShrinkRim: LiquidGlassSettings.backdropShrinkRim
  (0 to 1, default 0 = the upstream behaviour, bit for bit: the shader
  branch is skipped). The backdrop shrinks about the nearest point of a
  line through the material center along the longer side of the layer's
  glass bounds, rim x (long side - short side) long, instead of about
  the center: at 1 a capsule minifies by depth below its rim, as UIKit's
  lifted lens does. New uniform uBackdropShrinkAxis (vec2, float indices
  63-64, written with the common uniforms and on geometry bind);
  liquid_glass_settings.dart, rendering/liquid_glass_layer.dart,
  assets/shaders/liquid_glass_final_render_core.glsl.
  backdropSamplingReach still assumes the center (an over-estimate).
- 2026-10-03 moved into the package: imports rewritten to
  package:morph/src/glass/renderer/, flutter/material swapped for
  flutter/widgets (GlassGlow's default glow is Color(0x3DFFFFFF), the
  value of Colors.white24), a catch clause given its `on Object`, asset
  keys under packages/morph/, the bundle renamed morph_glass.shaderbundle,
  dart format.
- 2026-10-03 web stubs: the three final-render .frag files compile to an
  empty shader under SKIA_GRAPHICS_BACKEND (the web's SkSL compiler
  rejects the core's texture sampling: "Only simple shader sampling is
  supported"); the web never draws liquid glass.
- 2026-10-03 field geometry: LiquidGlassLayer.field (GlassField,
  glass_field.dart) - a sampled signed distance field of one body its
  owner fused already; the geometry pass then runs
  shaders/gpu/geometry_field_fragment.glsl (new bundle entry
  GeometryFieldFragment) instead of the shape pass: the same matte
  encoding, distance / normal / half thickness interpolated bilinearly
  from an RGBA32F texture of the field's nodes (sampled nearest, so no
  float filtering is needed), uploaded through a small ring of
  host-visible textures written again only three frames after their
  last use. The material pass still reads the shapes.
- 2026-10-03 fake glass draws the fused outline: GlassField.outline (the
  traced zero contour, layer coordinates) is handed by LiquidGlassLayer to
  ConsolidatedFakeGlassLayer (`outline`), which then clips its backdrop
  and surfaces to it and tints the part no shape covers (the neck) like
  the first shape; without an outline it is upstream's per-shape union.
